[48.512679, "o", "+\"\"\"Read one station's raw daily file and turn it into the standard daily inputs used by ``fao56.et0_daily``.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.512695, "o", "> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.512722, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.512746, "o", "> "]
[48.512997, "o", "+The raw files use the column names described in ``/app/docs/METHOD.md``.  This module converts those raw\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.513024, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.513252, "o", "+measurements into the *standard* units expected by the FAO‑56 implementation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.513273, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.513294, "o", "> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.513314, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.513431, "o", "+* Temperatures are already provided in °C.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.513457, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.513735, "o", "+* Relative humidity or dew‑point is converted to actual vapour pressure (kPa) using the helper functions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.513762, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.513835, "o", "+  in :pymod:`et0.fao56`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.51386, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.513886, "o", "> "]
[48.514151, "o", "+* Wind speed may be measured at an anemometer height other than 2 m.  When ``station.wind_height_m`` differs\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514161, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.514191, "o", "> "]
[48.514365, "o", "+  from 2 m, the FAO‑56 wind‑speed adjustment (Eq. 47) is applied:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514395, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514422, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.514539, "o", "+  ``u2 = u_z * (4.87 / log(67.8*z - 5.42))``\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514567, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514594, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.51473, "o", "+  where ``z`` is the measurement height in metres.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.514758, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.515085, "o", "+* Solar radiation can be supplied either in MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ (the standard) or in W m⁻².  When the latter is used we\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.515113, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[48.515495, "o", "+  convert to MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ by multiplying by 0.0864 (1 W m⁻² sustained for a day = 86 400 J m⁻² = 0.0864 MJ m⁻²).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[48.515505, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[48.515539, "o", "> "]
