[269.847205, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.847223, "o", "> "]
[269.847492, "o", "\"\"\"Read one station's raw daily file and turn it into the standard daily inputs used by ``fao56.et0_daily``.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.847512, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.847528, "o", "> +\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.847548, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.847564, "o", "> "]
[269.847826, "o", "+The raw files use the column names described in ``/app/docs/METHOD.md``. This module converts those raw\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.847849, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.847888, "o", "> "]
[269.848081, "o", "+measurements into the *standard* units expected by the FAO‑56 implementation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.848101, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.848116, "o", "> "]
[269.84813, "o", "+\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.84816, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.848174, "o", "> "]
[269.848278, "o", "+* Temperatures are already provided in °C.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.848297, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.848313, "o", "> "]
[269.848582, "o", "+* Relative humidity or dew‑point is converted to actual vapour pressure (kPa) using the helper functions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.848602, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.848617, "o", "> "]
[269.848676, "o", "+  in :pymod:`et0.fao56`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.848696, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.848709, "o", "> "]
[269.848993, "o", "+* Wind speed may be measured at an anemometer height other than 2 m. When ``station.wind_height_m`` differs\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.849012, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.849026, "o", "> "]
[269.849225, "o", "+  from 2 m, the FAO‑56 wind‑speed adjustment (Eq. 47) is applied:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.849244, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[269.849493, "o", "+  ``u2 = u_z * (4.87 / log(67.8*z - 5.42))`` where ``z`` is the measurement height in metres.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.849513, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.849533, "o", "> "]
[269.849848, "o", "+* Solar radiation can be supplied either in MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ (the standard) or in W m⁻². When the latter is used\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.849868, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.849881, "o", "> "]
[269.850273, "o", "+  we convert to MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ by multiplying by 0.0864 (1 W m⁻² sustained for a day = 86 400 J m⁻² = 0.0864 MJ m⁻²).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.850291, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.850306, "o", "> "]
[269.85032, "o", "+\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.850336, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.850343, "o", "> "]
[269.850618, "o", "+These conversions make the pipeline robust for any station register that follows the formats described in the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.850637, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.850652, "o", "> "]
[269.850696, "o", "+method document.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.850724, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.850739, "o", "> "]
[269.850754, "o", "+\"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[269.850769, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[269.850786, "o", "> \r\n"]
